- Adapted into `skills/bk-review/references/security-lens.md` from `plugins/security-guidance/hooks/review_api.py` and `plugins/security-guidance/hooks/patterns.py` (read 2026-09-24): the investigation method (entry points and sinks, following returns, sibling paths, the gate against the action, validator and consumer), the patterns reviews miss most, the refute pass and what is not a finding. The plugin ships its own `LICENSE`, byte-identical to the Apache License 2.0 at the repository root (compared 2026-09-24), and no `NOTICE`. The hooks that run it, the model calls, their schemas and tool budget, the diff size cap and the regexes are not carried.
- Adapted into `skills/bk-test/references/characterization.md` from `plugins/code-modernization/agents/test-engineer.md` (read 2026-09-26): the existing code as the oracle, literal inputs and outputs, every branch and boundary, tests that run from day one, fake secrets, and comments read as data. The plugin ships its own `LICENSE`, byte-identical to the Apache License 2.0 at the repository root, and no `NOTICE`. The dual-run harness against a legacy and a modern implementation and the modernization folder layout are not carried.
- Adapted into `skills/bk-build/references/major-upgrade.md` from `plugins/code-modernization/commands/modernize-uplift.md`, `plugins/code-modernization/agents/version-delta-analyst.md` and `plugins/code-modernization/agents/uplift-migrator.md` (read 2026-09-26): the pinned version pair, the question whether the tests run on the target, the four-kind delta catalog with silent behaviour as test-before-touch, the baseline recorded before any edit, the pilot and its recipe, the minimal diff, the proof against the baseline and the record of deferred work. The plugin ships its own `LICENSE`, byte-identical to the Apache License 2.0 at the repository root, and no `NOTICE`. The workflow scripts and their fan-out, the modernization folder layout, the brief and preflight files, the plugin's other agents and its per-stack tool lists are not carried.
- Nothing is vendored from `claude-code-setup` in the same repository, and on present evidence nothing will be: it was read in full on 2026-09-15 and inventoried at zero items absorbed, because it recommends host-specific automation and MCP servers the kit does not install. The reasoning is in `docs/specs/2026-09-11-skill-inventory.md`; whether the source stays ideas-only is the owner's call.

